  "title": "Pig War: Why Did Two Empires Nearly Fight Over a Pig?",
  "description": "Pig War: in 1859, one dead pig on San Juan Island pushed the United States and Britain to the edge of war. How did a quarrel in a potato patch end with hundreds of soldiers facing British warships?\n\nAmerican farmer Lyman Cutlar shot a Hudson's Bay Company pig that kept digging up his potatoes. Both nations claimed the San Juan Islands, so the border dispute exploded, until British Rear Admiral Baynes refused to start a war over a pig. The two armies then shared the island for about 12 years, and in 1872 an arbitration under Kaiser Wilhelm I gave it to the United States.\n\nSubscribe to Stickstory for one strange true story every day. Would you have shot the pig? Tell me in the comments!\n\n#shorts #pigwar #weirdhistory #stickstory",
